Explanation of the changes:

1. We keep the existing SequenceFlow/MessageFlow replacement logic untouched.
2. Immediately afterward, we check for `bpmn:Association`.
3. If the association’s visual parent (`connection.parent`) no longer matches the parent of one of its endpoints (`source.parent` or `target.parent`), we:
   - Remove the old (now–wrongly parented) connection.
   - Recreate it via `modeling.connect(…)`, which uses the correct shape container as semantic and DI parent.

With this in place, dragging both ends of an association out of a subprocess (or any container) will correctly reparent it, preventing its accidental deletion when the old container is removed.
